For more than a handful of students, import the class from a spreadsheet instead of
[adding them one at a time](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student).

## The one thing that catches everyone

**The importer reads columns by position, not by heading.** It skips your first row on the
assumption that it is a header, then reads column A as Student ID, column B as RFID, and so on —
whatever your headings actually say.

So a spreadsheet with the right headings in the wrong order imports silently and wrongly. Get the
order right and the headings can say anything you like.

## The column order

| Column | Field | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A | Student ID | Digits only, unique across the institute |
| B | RFID | The attendance card number; leave blank if cards come later |
| C | Full Name | |
| D | Date of Birth | `YYYY-MM-DD`. May be left blank |
| E | Class ID | The **Class Name** exactly as it appears in Classes |
| F | Email | |
| G | Mobile Number | Attendance SMS and payment reminders go here |
| H | Address | |
| I | Parent/Guardian | |
| J | Religion | |
| K | Nationality | |
| L | Gender | |

Every column after A–C may be left empty. An empty cell imports as empty; it does not stop the row.

## Steps

1. Prepare the sheet in the column order above, with one header row at the top.
2. Open **Students → Classes** and open the class you are importing into.
3. Open the **⋮ More options** menu and choose **Import Students from Excel**.
4. Pick your `.xlsx` or `.xls` file.
5. The **Imported Data Preview** table appears, showing every row exactly as the importer read it.
   **This is the checkpoint** — scroll across and confirm the values landed under the right
   headings. If names are showing up under "Date of Birth", your column order is wrong: cancel, fix
   the sheet, and start again.
6. Confirm to save.

If you see **Unable to import Excel file. Please try again.**, the file could not be parsed at all —
usually a `.csv` renamed to `.xlsx`, or a file still open in Excel.

## After importing

- Students imported without an RFID will not register attendance until a card number is added.
  Fill them in by editing each student, or re-import once cards are issued.
- Verify the count on the class roster matches your sheet before moving on.

